# The token mint's PTY runner, when the run sits at a real terminal (issue
# #187). The claude CLI holds its PTY in raw mode and DISCARDS the ^C byte, and
# under raw passthrough no layer turns the key into a signal — so `interact`
# binds the byte HERE, one layer out, before it is forwarded: the binding ends
# the child and answers 130, the way an interrupt ends any other command. Every
# other keystroke passes through untouched, which is what keeps the
# paste-the-code prompt answerable.
#
# Everything the child draws is appended to the capture file the caller made
# (600 before a byte is written — workkit.sh's mint owns its lifecycle). The
# command and the capture arrive through the environment: run_under_pty speaks
# for both callers, and the mint's words carry no spaces (workkit.sh says why).
log_file -a $env(WK_PTY_CAPTURE)
spawn {*}[split $env(WK_PTY_CMD) " "]
interact {
  "\003" { catch { exec kill [exp_pid] }; exit 130 }
  eof return
}
exit [lindex [wait] 3]
